    },
    {
      "id": "claim_874ebc5656854cf088fd9b1693a31e07",
      "statement": "The ten-second startup bound in Git.StartAsync covers only SyncMainAsync: EnsureRepositoryAsync runs all of its git commands with CancellationToken.None, so the repository identity checks are unbounded and can block host startup indefinitely.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L27-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:04743b75adf9aacca2db0a3dab0e92cd4445e827ee28e392050812fdb3b2eaf8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_66192028888d490ebbfc562002fc685b",
      "statement": "Git.SyncMainAsync never throws: a non-null FindMirrorProblemAsync result logs LogSyncSkipped at Warning and returns, InvalidOperationException is caught and logged at Warning by LogSyncFailed, and OperationCanceledException (the ten-second bound or shutdown) is caught and logged at Debug by LogSyncCancelled. A push to any ref other than exactly refs/heads/main, or a branch deletion, returns before the try block and logs no skip.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L107-L151",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:05ef875c7ad6b67604a7f823634f5beca8f5f4dd5854f8fcb171ca2e25834ea2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_15df3c1b6a6c428fa754f7e9f1ab12ae",
      "statement": "FindMirrorProblemAsync is consumed with opposite policies by its two callers: Git.SyncMainAsync logs the problem as a Warning and continues so startup and push deliveries never fail, while ImplementSpec.PrepareWorkspaceAsync rethrows it as an InvalidOperationException so no agent starts on an unacceptable base.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L78-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d58869dfb51b549f616cff81809feec46d59c0a2a5660a893cc06c0da80fd8f1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L124-L129",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:72f449acf8c56f038ec128feaab93220205d4c2cb7de7e9560b9d4073869514d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2749b0689b644244a5865fe0faaf420f",
      "statement": "Git.RunAsync creates every child git process with GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 so credential prompts fail fast, and on cancellation calls TryKill with entireProcessTree: true before rethrowing the OperationCanceledException, leaving the caller to decide the outcome.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L180-L230",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:532213264b2565e224e6b590ddf13173334aad5e35e1f72acc9ca36e2593c279:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d8d6802c158e458ca191debc34c4534f",
      "statement": "TryKill guards only InvalidOperationException ('process already exited'), so any other Kill failure (for example Win32Exception) escapes the cancellation handler as a different exception type and is recorded by JobQueue's general catch as a job failure rather than being treated as shutdown cancellation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L63-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b84e82f4ccb6ada4ce8ca7da595cb6395a2aa5ac9cddbdfcdefc455dcd2efeb:"
