    {
      "id": "claim_845132d102b3474a9f789422a41bf375",
      "statement": "ImplementSpec.PrepareWorkspaceAsync throws rather than degrading on three conditions - Git.Repository is null because the Git hosted service has not started, the issue owner/repository differ from the parsed origin, or FindMirrorProblemAsync returns a reason - and each throw prevents the agent from ever being constructed for that job.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L63-L110",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d1adcc5d278f63232d4ed568e5782aa0cd3c69d10eee1cd5850c4d89195203fc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ea173275ad0447a795ae42a100a22129",
      "statement": "ImplementSpec.RunAsync contains no catch block: cancellation and exceptions propagate out of preparation, the agent session, the agent run, and the trailing GetStatusAsync call, unwinding through the chat client disposal finally and the await-using role disposal before reaching JobQueue. LogCompleted is therefore a success-only record, so a run that fails after the agent responded produces no completion line despite leaving work in the worktree.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L134-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea6cd1b17c509cf336822a997c7b7c67972107c332c584b8e6ebd246be79eb58:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L28-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:53f9fb148752070c9dbfbaa10f3d40be30a9d3a8cd1fe886893e5b3efe5a177c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_df900003bdd9424d9ec51f6a72b8526e",
      "statement": "JobQueue isolates each job with three clauses: a filtered catch (OperationCanceledException) when stoppingToken.IsCancellationRequested that swallows shutdown cancellations silently, a general catch that logs LogFailed at Error level with the message 'Job {Key} failed', and a finally that removes the in-flight key. A failed job is never requeued, gets no attempt count, and does not block its key.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L41-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f45a34a34cae6e11b500273221d2bac01f0738d8f1bd4eb8647c496e2203c122:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9f44697888ed42bda544aaedb4e65bfb",
      "statement": "A failed job produces no GitHub-visible signal: ImplementSpec resolves Git, IOptions<SebastianConfig>, ProviderResolver and ILogger but never GitHubService, and the only two GitHub write operations (PostCommentAsync, CloseIssueAsync) are called exclusively from GitHubWebhookProcessor's invalid-spec path, so a job that fails leaves the issue sitting in ready-for-agent with an Error log line as its only evidence.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L28-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48e54d5c38dc112dbf2c5bf20845e3330966fc8e0a606bc5a624bf88cf72f2a7:"
