    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0a37cbfb76b44b58a02200733bf71ac3",
      "statement": "JobQueue.StopAsync completes the channel writer and then delegates to the base class, which cancels the loop rather than draining it: new admissions return false with their key rolled back, buffered never-started jobs are abandoned while still holding their in-flight keys, and running jobs observe cancellation that neither catch logs because both are filtered on stoppingToken.IsCancellationRequested. Program.cs does not configure HostOptions.ShutdownTimeout, so the framework default bounds how long a cancellation-ignoring job can run.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Program.cs#L11-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:55c780b60958294912167d4df7ef03f84d978eb4acaf0f5d177a37bcbb41a099:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Jobs/JobQueue.cs#L35-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c480ecc8edfca579c430edf5997575a6f03598fd5a08d2e923cdf99a740f0249:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_08cd79916ce64f72af8b2f062e8ddfb4",
      "statement": "The documented index.lock race is accepted by design: the static PrepareLock serializes only preparation against preparation, while the push-webhook SyncMainAsync takes no semaphore, so a concurrent 'git merge --ff-only' and 'git worktree add' can contend on .git/index.lock. Whichever process loses exits non-zero, failing that one job (or the webhook) while git's own locking keeps the repository consistent; the code states this in a shortcut comment rather than closing the race, which would block a webhook request behind up to ten job preparations.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L23-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0576f1b593e9868ab2b453e66c149e20168af01fd386b5f8b9e124a0220ee8c7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L118-L119",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c480724a19eaf2f3a590a2b8f817a3eebbed4a40faaa5c70e73dfee35d3b93dc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Webhooks/GitHubWebhookProcessor.cs#L107-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:157fae54eb39a767fcaa9562bc592d1cfa5a6be5dadf7c984f9a08e5a9cc7400:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_da524eac6a4c4d12b9d52b82a2d4ad11",
      "statement": "The test suite pins the failure policies that matter most but not the sync or shutdown paths: JobQueueTests' ContinuesAfterJobFailure proves a throwing job neither escapes the handler nor stops the loop, RejectsDuplicateKeyWhileJobRuns proves the key is held for the run and released in the finally, RunsAtMostTenJobsConcurrently proves the concurrency cap, and ImplementSpecTests' RejectsDirtyMain and RejectsForeignRepository prove two of the three preparation throws plus the two worktree reuse behaviors. Nothing covers SyncMainAsync, the JobQueue cancellation filters, admission after StopAsync, buffered-job abandonment, the intake GitHub calls, or the webhook processor.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/Sebastian.Tests/Agent/ImplementSpecTests.cs#L7-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dcf1bda3471d8b06a98367c87966f09afd434f30378f12a087bba5c78ca844e4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/Sebastian.Tests/Jobs/JobQueueTests.cs#L44-L90",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c70440b121a7bb39d7492855548495d20564bed549034c157520b2ebca1c9ecf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_aa39fe42f310496aa85f3d42c341c9fa",
      "statement": "Log levels make the diagnosis path asymmetric: the only Information-level outcomes in the whole pipeline are the arrival of a delivery, 'Started implementation', and 'Implementation completed'; every failure-to-progress outcome is lower - duplicate suppression, invalid-spec closure, and a cancelled mirror sync are Debug, and mirror problems or sync git failures are Warning - so at default verbosity an issue that never started cannot be told apart from one that was filtered before enqueue.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L134-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea6cd1b17c509cf336822a997c7b7c67972107c332c584b8e6ebd246be79eb58:"
        },
